  "description": "UCUBAY crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group P 2 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C40 H88 Dy9 N4 O49 5+,5(Cl1 O4 1-),24(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy10 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy13 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy14 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy15 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy16 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy17 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy18 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 36 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.611-5.132 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.44-161.96°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9(μ4-O)(μ3-OH)8(LH)4(OAc)4(H2O)12]·5ClO4·24H2O (LH = doubly deprotonated Chromogen I, C8H11NO5; elemental Dy9C40H136N4O93Cl5). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 12 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
